1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,173
Business questions deserve numbers you can trust.

2
00:00:03,213 --> 00:00:07,304
Meet Ask the Warehouse, built on Oracle AI Database.

3
00:00:07,794 --> 00:00:14,198
In our synthetic demo, Florida turnover is one point eight nine percent under the approved definition.

4
00:00:14,238 --> 00:00:19,031
Count internal transfers and it rises to two point three three percent.

5
00:00:19,071 --> 00:00:20,642
Same data, different meaning.

6
00:00:21,132 --> 00:00:28,279
Each certified result shows its definition, owner, version, source view, compiled SQL and binds.

7
00:00:28,319 --> 00:00:30,332
Oracle records answer provenance.

8
00:00:30,822 --> 00:00:33,526
The query path is deliberately fixed.

9
00:00:33,566 --> 00:00:38,558
A request chooses an approved metric; it never becomes executable SQL.

10
00:00:39,048 --> 00:00:42,098
New metrics start as drafts in Oracle.

11
00:00:42,138 --> 00:00:44,746
A reviewer validates the source contract.

12
00:00:44,786 --> 00:00:49,160
A different approver certifies the version before it becomes available.

13
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:55,994
Location grants keep each user inside the data they are allowed to see, even when a question asks for more.

14
00:00:56,484 --> 00:00:59,863
Select AI can help explore candidate questions.

15
00:00:59,903 --> 00:01:04,748
The certified path uses reviewed, bound SQL for official answers.

16
00:01:05,238 --> 00:01:10,589
Connect your own Oracle schema, map a source view, and ship governed answers.

17
00:01:10,629 --> 00:01:12,662
Ask the Warehouse, on GitHub.
